Report a damaged shared-string table or styles part.

Both are parsed in full before the worksheet is opened, through
expat_process_zip_file(), whose "did this part parse?" answer upstream has
commented out: it returns 0 whatever happened. A shared-string table cut
short loaded as far as the cut, and a styles part with broken XML or a bad
CRC-32 loaded partially or not at all, so strings went missing and dates
read as plain numbers, with nothing to say so.

expat_process_zip_file_checked() is the same function returning what
happened: not found, not well-formed XML (with the line), or a ZIP size or
CRC-32 mismatch, which miniz checks when the member is closed.
expat_process_zip_file() keeps its old answer for every other caller. The
first failure among the two parts is kept on the sheet handle, and
xlsxioread_sheet_finish() reports it, ahead of anything the worksheet itself
did, as XLSXIOREAD_SHEET_ERROR_PART_XML or _PART_ZIP;
xlsxioread_sheet_error_part() names the part.

Written for zuxlsx (#38). None of it is upstream.

